## 1. The Big Idea

_One sentence: **A prescription sleep drug is a 30-day engineered bridge that carries you across a wrecked sleep pattern and back onto the foundation you built in Parts 1–3 — its cables are the habits being tensioned as you cross, its far end is a deliberate off-ramp, and beside it stands the collapsed false crossing (Z-drugs/benzos) that never reaches the other side.** The poster makes the reader feel, instantly, that the drug is temporary infrastructure with a planned dismantling date — and that a bridge anchored to nothing relapses the moment you step off._

